{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The early-1960s collection and Rick Nelson's greatest hits fit the familiar, melodic oldies I have been choosing through AM Gold and other compilations.",
    "Fleetwood Mac's hits fit my interest in accessible classic-rock favorites, while Poems, Prayers and Promises appeals to the gentle folk songwriting I enjoy in Simon & Garfunkel and Jonathan Edwards."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Blues Of Desperation feels less suited to my current interest in melodic oldies and familiar songs; an overlap with rock alone does not make it appealing today.",
    "John Denver's live concert interests me less than a studio collection right now, and Sarah McLachlan's reflective pop does not connect as closely with the older folk and classic-rock favorites I want.",
    "Remasters and 5 Original Albums leave me unsure which music I would get. I also need to confirm the artist and songs on 1 Remixed/Remastered before choosing it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in classic rock seems to have been stretched into an interest in blues-focused music, although familiar melodies matter more to me today.",
    "A collection or remastered release is not appealing just because of its format; I still need to recognize the artist or want the songs it contains."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of best-of albums and oldies compilations reflect a wish to revisit recognizable songs and rediscover forgotten hits.",
    "Gentle folk songwriting is a specific connection for me, and today I would explore it through studio recordings before a live concert."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in oldies, folk and classic-rock collections, but sometimes stretched that interest beyond the familiar songs and specific musical connections I want today."
}"}
